   "file": "projects.md",
   "heading": "Adaptive Low-Power Temperature Monitor (Arduino, individual coursework)",
   "text": "Adaptive Low-Power Temperature Monitor (Arduino, individual coursework). I built an Arduino data logger that adjusts its sampling rate using an on-board DFT and the Nyquist criterion. I cut the sampling rate by 50% (from 1 Hz to about 0.5 Hz) on a slow signal, within an estimated 1.5 KB of the board's 2 KB of SRAM. I logged the data over serial and analysed it in Python. The code is on GitHub.",
